^FX Small UPC-E label, 1.25 x 1 inch (254 x 203 dots at 203 dpi).
^FX Shows the tiny label for a small package such as a lip balm: a black band that says SAMPLE, the product name and
^FX price, and a UPC-E bar code, the short form of a UPC-A that fits a small pack.
^FX This is the one sample with number system 0: UPC-E can only shorten numbers of that system, so the number is
^FX invented and the label says SAMPLE in plain text.
^FX Sample label from LabelScope. All data is made up.
^XA
^PW254
^LL203
^LH0,0
^FX Black band with reversed text.
^FO10,8^GB234,34,34,B^FS
^FO78,12^FR^A0N,26,26^FDSAMPLE^FS
^FX Product name and price.
^FO12,52^A0N,26,26^FDLip balm^FS
^FO152,48^A0N,34,34^FD$1.99^FS
^FX UPC-E bar code of a ten digit number that shortens to six digits: 51 modules at 3 dots, 153 dots wide. The system
^FX digit 0 sits in the quiet zone on the left and the check digit on the right.
^BY3,3,60
^FO46,92^B9N,60,Y,N,Y^FD1234500005^FS
^XZ
